(Bug #59 through a call. A `list` parameter has no proven element type, so
 its loop variable is runtime-tagged exactly like a mixed list literal's -
 and a `treating` clause in the function body must dispatch on that tag,
 not on the parameter's static type.)

To announce with a list called things.
  print each thing from things treating "a" as "b".

announce of [1, "a"].
announce of ["a", "a"].
